          "speed",
          "distance",
          "time"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Speed is the distance travelled in one unit of time. Speed equals distance divided by time. A bus covering 100 km in 2 hours has a speed of 50 km per hour.\nWe measure distance with a ruler, tape or odometer and time with a clock or stopwatch.\nA faster object covers more distance in the same time."
        }
